Feature: Flight modes
  M steps through MANUAL, ANGLE (self-levelling) and ACRO (rate), and back to MANUAL. The
  plane starts in MANUAL. The calibration wizard ignores it, like every other button.

  Expectation: MANUAL to ANGLE
    Given the flight mode is MANUAL
    And the calibration wizard is closed
    When the pilot presses flight mode
    Then the flight mode is ANGLE

  Expectation: ANGLE to ACRO
    Given the flight mode is ANGLE
    And the calibration wizard is closed
    When the pilot presses flight mode
    Then the flight mode is ACRO

  Expectation: ACRO back to MANUAL
    Given the flight mode is ACRO
    And the calibration wizard is closed
    When the pilot presses flight mode
    Then the flight mode is MANUAL
